    "explanation": "This case goes to a human reviewer. The $36.60 fare is held - neither refunded nor confirmed - and no compensation is paid. Here is the reasoning, for both of you.\n\nTo the rider: your central point is correct. The booked optimal route was 14.0 km (EV-TRIP-00107) and the GPS trace runs 17.57 km (EV-GPS-00107), an excess of 3.57 km, or 25.5%, so both POL-RD-01 gates (over 0.8 km and over 20%) pass and the deviation is ESTABLISHED on the trace figure, which governs over the rounded 17.6 km copy on the trip record. The driver's 'jam' answer does not excuse it: POL-RD-03 requires a traffic advisory naming the affected road with a validity window, and no advisory was issued that evening (EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT); a general assertion that traffic was bad, naming no advisory, carries no weight under POL-RD-08. POL-RD-04 does not apply (the chat holds no rider instruction to detour - the only two messages are mid-trip), nor POL-RD-05 (no amended pickup or dropoff), nor POL-RD-11 (the fare is METERED, not an upfront quote), nor POL-RD-12 (not a pooled trip). No POL-RD-09 pass-through or billing-integrity correction arises: the fare breakdown has no ERP gantries, no tolls, no airport surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo. The deviation is not MATERIAL (25.5% is under 50%, 3.57 km under 8.0 km) and there is no repeat-deviation pattern (1 flag against 619 completed trips), so there is no POL-RD-06 full-refund uplift and no driver-conduct referral.\n\nWhy I cannot decide it here: the size of the excess rests on a single artifact, the GPS trace EV-GPS-00107, which the admissibility pre-pass has down-weighted to 0.30 and tagged with GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a 331.8 m multipath jump on the final Raffles Place approach, implying impossible speeds). Two things must be said of it, as the policy requires. First, it is impaired at the schema level and its weight is 0.30. Second, it is NOT impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 - there is no gap over 90 s, its worst jump is 331.8 m (under the 500 m limb) and it samples every 10 s - so a deviation may properly be established on it, and it is. The difficulty is POL-GEN-02(2): my confidence cannot exceed the lowest weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact, and here nothing independent carries it. The excess distance is the deciding fact. The trip record's 17.6 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement, which POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test; the fare's 17.6 km is the same measurement on the meter. The driver's admissions - 'cte very jam tonight boss' in the chat and 'I went by Newton and Kim Seng' in his statement - are real corroboration of the ROUTE and they satisfy the extra corroboration POL-RD-08 demands because of the rider's 60-day claim history, but neither supplies an independent MEASUREMENT of the distance. Confidence is therefore capped at 0.30, below the 0.70 platform floor, and POL-RD-10(1) makes escalation mandatory and terminal. POL-RD-10(3) does not fire, precisely because the trace is not policy-impaired. Had confidence permitted a ruling, POL-RD-02 would give: charged_total $36.60; recomputed_fare ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + $0.80 = $29.177; refund $7.45 (the 1.35 multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, the only artifact carrying it). That figure is not payable now.\n\nTo the driver: I have not accepted your traffic explanation, which names no advisory and carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and your submission that the 0.30 weight caps confidence and compels escalation under POL-GEN-02(2) and POL-RD-10(1) is the reason this case cannot be decided here. Your other points stand: the excess is below both materiality limbs, so no POL-RD-06 uplift or referral, and there are no charge lines to correct under POL-RD-09.\n\nWhat would settle it, for the reviewer: a drift-corrected or clean trace over the final approach, or any independent measurement of the distance driven - for example a rider-side track, or a distance the platform derived independently of this trace. On that evidence the $7.45 figure can be confirmed or adjusted."
